nsition normally.\"\n  },\n  \"scan_execution_order\": [\n    {\n      \"stage\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"Edge sampling\",\n      \"action\": \"Sample each input once. All inputs are level-sensitive; no edge detection is required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"Safety/reset priority and state transitions\",\n      \"action\": \"Read previous_direction as the retained pre-state. Set desired_direction to 0 if Stop is true or the button levels are equal, to 1 if only ForwardButton is true, and to -1 if only ReverseButton is true. Apply the state transition table to select output_direction, then store it as previous_direction. Stop clears direction memory but is not latched.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF\",\n      \"action\": \"No timer FBs are required or called; the neutral interval is exactly one invocation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": 4,\n      \"name\": \"Unified output assignments\",\n      \"action\": \"Assign Forward := (output_direction = 1) and Reverse := (output_direction = -1) once. Observe these outputs at the end of the same scan.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"formal_assertions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A1\",\n      \"formula\": \"G(!(Forward & Reverse))\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A2\",\n      \"formula\": \"G((Stop | (ForwardButton <-> ReverseButton)) -> (!Forward & !Reverse))\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A3\",\n      \"formula\": \"G((Reverse & X(!Stop & ForwardButton & !ReverseButton)) -> X(!Forward & !Reverse))\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A4\",\n      \"formula\": \"G((Forward & X(!Stop & !ForwardButton & ReverseButton)) -> X(!Forward & !Reverse))\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A5\",\n      \"formula\": \"G((!Reverse & X(!Stop & ForwardButton & !ReverseButton)) -> X(Forward))\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A6\",\n      \"formula\": \"G((!Forward & X(!Stop & !ForwardButton & ReverseButton)) -> X(Reverse))\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
